<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: EU-Japan summit set for Sept 30.</title>
<headline>EU-Japan summit set for Sept 30.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union said on Monday it would hold its fifth annual summit meeting with Japan in Tokyo on September 30.</p>
<p>European Commission President Jacques Santer and Irish Prime Minister John Bruton will meet Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto, according to a statement issued by the EU Presidency in Dublin on behalf of the 15-nation bloc.</p>
<p>Bruton is president-in-office of the European Council during Ireland's six-month tenure as EU president.</p>
<p>&quot;The summit will provide an opportunity for a broad exchange of views on the current state of EU-Japan relations and on the international situation,&quot; the EU said.</p>
<p>The previous EU-Japan summit took place in Paris in June 1995.</p>
</text>
